From: OHOS SPDK port
Subject: [PATCH] Gate the DIX encryption sequence on its ISA-L crypto dependency

Like test_sequence_crypto, test_sequence_dix creates a software AES-XTS
key. Without ISA-L crypto, initialization returns -ENOTSUP and its fatal
assertion leaks an I/O channel, leaving suite cleanup spinning forever.
Apply the existing feature gate to this case too. No assertion is changed;
this disabled-feature case is excluded, not reported as passed. The separate
DIX generation/verification sequence test remains enabled.

--- a/test/unit/lib/accel/accel.c/accel_ut.c
+++ b/test/unit/lib/accel/accel.c/accel_ut.c
@@ -4188,6 +4188,7 @@
 	poll_threads();
 }
 
+#ifdef SPDK_CONFIG_ISAL_CRYPTO
 static void
 test_sequence_dix(void)
 {
@@ -4335,6 +4336,8 @@
 	spdk_put_io_channel(ioch);
 	poll_threads();
 }
+
+#endif /* SPDK_CONFIG_ISAL_CRYPTO */
 
 static int
 test_sequence_setup(void)
@@ -4427,7 +4430,9 @@
 	CU_ADD_TEST(seq_suite, test_sequence_same_iovs);
 	CU_ADD_TEST(seq_suite, test_sequence_crc32);
 	CU_ADD_TEST(seq_suite, test_sequence_dix_generate_verify);
+#ifdef SPDK_CONFIG_ISAL_CRYPTO /* DIX sequence creates a software AES-XTS key */
 	CU_ADD_TEST(seq_suite, test_sequence_dix);
+#endif
 
 	suite = CU_add_suite("accel", test_setup, test_cleanup);
 	CU_ADD_TEST(suite, test_spdk_accel_task_complete);
